{"schema_version": 4, "name": "s1-metabolic-partnership", "investigation": "eukaryogenesis", "created": "2026-10-27", "title": "S1 \u2014 Metabolic partnership: can an archaeal-bacterial pair gain fitness from exchange?", "phase": "Design", "status": "planned", "design_status": "drafted", "simulation_status": "not_run", "evaluation_status": "not_evaluated", "gate_status": "not_started", "topic": "metabolic-coupling", "tags": ["symbiosis", "fba", "community", "cross-feeding", "bioenergetics"], "concept": "Syntrophy and mutualism made operational as exchange fluxes, partner-dependent growth, invasion fitness, and environmental contingencies. Curated candidate genomes -> gap-audited genome-scale models (GEMs) -> two-member community FBA / dynamic FBA, with separate positive and negative controls, under alternative redox and substrate regimes.", "question": "Can plausible archaeal-bacterial pairs gain fitness from metabolite exchange, and under which redox and substrate regimes? Does the predicted mutualism survive mass-balance and electron-donor/acceptor feasibility audits and alternative reconstructions?", "hypothesis": "Under at least one field-consistent redox/substrate regime, a reconstructed archaeal-host / bacterial-partner pair achieves partner-dependent growth (each grows better together than alone) on mass-balanced exchange fluxes, while a no-exchange / parasitic control does not.", "claim": "An archaeal-bacterial association can become mutually beneficial under restricted redox and substrate regimes \u2014 partner-dependent growth emerges on feasible, mass-balanced metabolite exchange \u2014 but the benefit is not necessarily stable or obligate, and it disappears outside the feasible regime and under alternative gap-fills.", "behavior_tests": [{"name": "partner-dependent-growth-feasible", "classification": "primary", "description": "The two-member community grows faster than either member alone (a positive cross-feeding advantage) in at least one redox/substrate regime.", "measure": {"kind": "derived_scalar", "path": "partner_dependent_growth_ratio"}, "pass_if": {"op": ">", "value": 1.1, "provenance": {"kind": "hypothesis", "note": "Ratio of community biomass flux to the best single-member flux; >1.1 = a >10% mutualistic advantage. Threshold is a pre-registered hypothesis to be calibrated against Imachi-2020 syntrophic growth once the GEMs are built."}}, "cites": ["imachi-nature-2020", "santana-molina-nee-2025"]}, {"name": "exchange-mass-balanced", "classification": "primary", "description": "Exchanged metabolites close an elemental mass/charge balance (no free lunch).", "measure": {"kind": "derived_scalar", "path": "exchange_mass_balance_residual"}, "pass_if": {"op": "approx", "value": 0.0, "tol": "1e-6", "provenance": {"kind": "theory", "note": "Exchange fluxes must conserve C/N/O/H and charge by construction."}}}], "acceptance_criteria": [{"behavior": "partner-dependent-growth-feasible"}], "literature_anchors": [{"expectation": "Syntrophic archaeal-bacterial growth is observed in Prometheoarchaeum syntrophicum.", "model_observable": "partner_dependent_growth_ratio", "source": "Imachi et al. 2020, Nature", "cites": ["imachi-nature-2020"], "status_in_workspace": "proposed"}], "parent_studies": [], "baseline": [{"name": "baseline", "composite": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community", "params": {"lineages": "fixer:4,reducer:4", "coupling": "shared", "model_proto_ecology": "reaction_universe"}, "note": "First-fidelity arm. metacommunity_robustness vs isolated_robustness give the partner-dependent advantage (partner_dependent_growth_ratio); C_residual_max gives exchange mass balance. The next-fidelity arm \u2014 two gap-audited archaeal/alphaproteobacterial GEMs under community FBA \u2014 is blocked on COBRApy (not installed) + genome reconstruction (GTDB/NCBI data not yet ingested)."}], "observables": ["community/metacommunity_robustness", "community/isolated_robustness", "ledger/C_residual_max"], "data_inputs": [{"name": "GTDB genomes", "use": "candidate Asgard + alphaproteobacterial genomes", "url": "https://gtdb.ecogenomic.org/downloads"}, {"name": "NCBI Assembly/RefSeq", "use": "CDS + protein annotations for organism selection", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/datasets/"}, {"name": "KEGG/MetaCyc/BiGG", "use": "reaction stoichiometry + pathway mappings for reconstruction", "url": "https://bigg.ucsd.edu/"}, {"name": "Comparative central metabolism (Zenodo)", "use": "curated proteomes/orthogroups/trees", "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10991068"}], "runs": [{"run_id": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793116359__8701ae", "spec_id": "s1-metabolic-partnership", "label": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793116359__8701ae", "sim_name": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793116359__8701ae", "variant": null, "composite": null, "params": {}, "n_steps": null, "status": "completed", "started_at": 1793116370.1587, "completed_at": 1793116370.1587, "generation_id": null, "source": "study.yaml", "started_at_iso": "2026-10-27T15:52:50Z", "stale": false, "params_summary": "", "outcomes": {"partner-dependent-growth-feasible": {"result": "SKIP", "evaluated_by": "agent", "note": "derived-scalar computer 'partner_dependent_growth_ratio' error: 'isolated_robustness'", "auto_evaluated": true}, "exchange-mass-balanced": {"result": "SKIP", "evaluated_by": "agent", "note": "unsupported op: 'approx'", "auto_evaluated": true}}, "computed_outcomes": {"partner-dependent-growth-feasible": {"evaluated_by": "agent", "reason": "observable 'partner_dependent_growth_ratio' not resolvable", "reconcile": "no_authored"}, "exchange-mass-balanced": {"evaluated_by": "agent", "reason": "unsupported op: 'approx'", "reconcile": "no_authored"}}, "provenance": {"params": {"coupling": {"value": "shared", "source"